## 6. Security and release hygiene
- Keep API keys and credentials out of Git.
- Ensure `.env` is ignored and provide `.env.example` with placeholder values only if needed.
- Avoid committing private or personally identifying customer data.
- Pin or document dependencies where practical.
- Confirm error messages do not expose secrets or local filesystem details.

